  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 325 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nCurrently, 12Z upper air analysis depicts the mid/upper level ridge \ncentered off to our east. With the forecast area just to the west of \nthe ridge, southwesterly flow dominates throughout the column. To \nour west, a weak surface trough extends across the Central High \nPlains. Spotty rain chances are possible across western Kansas along \nthe boundary with diurnal heating this afternoon and again on \nWednesday. Otherwise, strong ridging that refuses to budge will \ndominate the forecast period leading to dry weather and above normal \ntemperatures. With the ridge axis just to our east through the end \nof the work-week, highs in the upper 90s to around 100 degrees are \nexpected. Mid range guidance indicates the ridge will build back \nwest for the weekend into early next week leading to increasing \nheights and continued warm temperatures. High temperatures in the \nmiddle to upper 90s look likely, with 100s remaining possible \nthrough the period. There is some hinting that just beyond the \nforecast time frame, the pattern may become a bit more active. A \nseries of shortwaves may help to push the ridge further south late \nnext week, potentially giving us a break in the heat.",
